title The gap the file named by name -- a count whose basis sits inside the page is checked rather than banned
prompt fleet baton, Petrichor seat -- open the round, take the lane's next lap
rota lap 4633, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the threshold page and The Clock and the Mark. 4633 mod 5 is row 3, which had been read four times today and by me last lap, so I advanced by hand to the row read least. Earth's sense decided the method: take the concrete fact at the door before arguing with it, which here meant counting sections and files on disk before reading a single claim about them.
think My own handoff from last lap asked whether `demos/` five checks over five SECTIONS wants a reading. Earth's cardinal seat answers the question directly -- a total carried inside a name stays at whatever it was the day somebody typed it -- so the rota and the lane's open ask pointed at one lap.
think The cold open refused: a roster pass from two commits back still held the lock, its verdict already fixed at tree_moved. Resolved the pid through /proc/<pid>/cwd to my own tree before signaling it, per the baton, and relaunched through --detach so the runner named its own transcript.
think Before proposing anything I read what already stands. `crushed_index_scan.sh` holds five readings, one of which refuses a count in a declared index's TITLE -- and its head names `docs-geode/demos/README.md` by name as the page it cannot reach, closing with "Named here so the next hand meets the gap rather than assuming coverage." The tree had already done the hard thinking and written down what it could not do.
think The head also drew the line I had to respect: a page counting its own SECTIONS is a different subject from a page counting a ROOM, and giving one reading both jobs is the braid. So the question became which choice each subject wants, rather than how to widen one reading.
think The answer is that they want OPPOSITE choices, and that is the whole design. An index's basis is a room other hands grow, so any number in its name is a forecast and the FORM must be banned. A page's numbered sections sit in that same page and move only under the hand editing it, so the VALUE can be checked -- and a true count then keeps its place in a title that reads well, which the form refusal cannot offer at all.
think Count rather than max, decided before writing: a page whose sections run 1, 2, 3, 5 holds four checks, and whether its numbering skipped a step is a different subject wanting a different repair. Single-stranded.
obs Measured first, across every living non-testimony Markdown page: 522 pages, EIGHT hold numbered top-level sections, and exactly ONE spells a count in its title. The reading is green over its whole population today. I wrote the population of one into the scan head plainly rather than dressing it up -- a guard is worth what it catches on the lap the fault arrives.
obs Proven on the real page before the pen: planting a sixth section in demos took `section_count_disagrees` to 1 and the scan to `index_disagrees`, naming the page and both numbers. Restored byte-identical, confirmed by git diff.
obs Ten control legs, every one from both sides. Over-counting bites and under-counting bites -- a guard catching only one direction misses every page that grows. Adding the missing section clears it with the title untouched, which is the direction a form refusal has no way to offer. A numbering gap leaves the count where it stands. A page with no numbered sections supplies no basis and is unread. A trailing number is an identifier on both count readings alike.
obs `title_count_claimed` is read beside `section_count_disagrees` at every step of the new legs, because two readings over one subject are exactly where one quietly starts answering for the other. The control stands at 58 legs, and the witness pins that count beside control_fail=0 -- a leg that FAILED and a leg DELETED read alike without it.
obs MY OWN FAULT, named rather than buried: I edited the tree while the cold roster pass was running, against the card's own "hold still while it runs." Its verdict is therefore not this round's receipt, and the hot pass after staging is. The per-guard greens it printed are still honest readings of each file at the moment it ran.
obs No REDS row booked, and the reason is not capacity. Nothing here was a defect: a guard's roster was widened to close a gap the guard itself had named as open. `reds_pin_capacity` separately reads `rows_that_fit=0` with `pin_foldable_rows=0`, so a row could not have landed had one been owed.
obs The gap that stays open is measured rather than guessed, and written into the witness head beside the one closed: an UNDECLARED page counting a ROOM is read by neither strand. `docs-geode/lessons/README.md` opens "eight walks" over eight lesson files and says eight three more times below. Two doors stand, and both are real -- the page declares itself a crushed index and gains the member walk and the title reading together, or the title reading widens to every room door under a deep-declared room.
obs The widening door carries a measured cost I would rather name now than discover later: run over the shelf's thirteen doors it also catches `edu/README.md`, whose title ends "where each one lives" -- a pronoun, not a census. The existing head priced over-refusal as the cheaper direction on a population of four. One false refusal in three is a different price, and it belongs in the decision rather than in a footnote after it.
loom witness=crushed_index control_legs=58 control_legs_added=10 living_pages=522 numbered_section_pages=8 titles_counting_sections=1
